{
  "version": 1,
  "_comment": [
    "Authoring templates kept out of the GenStudio Editor tab's Game objects list.",
    "Hiding is presentation-only: every template here is still in the package, still",
    "builds, and is still reachable from scripts. It is not a delete or a permission.",
    "",
    "The Game objects list is the graph outliner's template listing: one flat row per",
    "`.hstf` in the project, titled from the file's basename. So",
    "Templates/Weapons/PistolVisual.hstf reads as `Pistol Visual`.",
    "These are scaffolding a creator never opens.",
    "",
    "`path` is the binding and the only field read. It is an exact project-relative",
    "path, so a template added to one of these folders later stays visible until it is",
    "named here.",
    "",
    "Only the two templates a creator opens are absent: space.hstf and",
    "Templates/PlayerCharacter.hstf.",
    "",
    "Consumed by DEVHorizonWorldsGenStudioHiddenAssets.js in www."
  ],
